NUM-37: let a rooftop disconnection with Rough or Slope = 0 overflow

roofFluxRates() called getSurfaceOverflowRate() when the roof has no
Manning outflow (Rough or Slope = 0) but threw its result away, so the
surface outflow, and the gutter flow taken from it, stayed 0 and all rain
piled up on the roof. Assign the overflow rate to SurfaceOutflow, as the
Manning branch does, so water above the storage depth leaves within the
step (the documented rule) and the gutters take up to their capacity of it.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply NUM-37_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/lidproc.c b/src/legacy/engine/lidproc.c
index dbd83e4..edfdf96 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/lidproc.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/lidproc.c
@@ -480,7 +480,7 @@ void roofFluxRates(double x[], double f[])
     SurfaceInfil = 0.0;
     if ( theLidProc->surface.alpha > 0.0 )
       SurfaceOutflow = getSurfaceOutflowRate(surfaceDepth);
-    else getSurfaceOverflowRate(&surfaceDepth);
+    else SurfaceOutflow = getSurfaceOverflowRate(&surfaceDepth);
     StorageDrain = MIN(theLidProc->drain.coeff/UCF(RAINFALL), SurfaceOutflow);
     SurfaceOutflow -= StorageDrain;
     f[SURF] = (SurfaceInflow - SurfaceEvap - StorageDrain - SurfaceOutflow);
